4.  THE FLAG'S PRICE: what Lemma H states against what A-17 carries
================================================================================================
  [OK ] Lemma H's toy N_leaf: got 12288
  [OK ] Lemma H's toy N_node: got 12283
  [OK ] Lemma H's toy N_overlap (leaf+node 64-byte objects): got 24571
  C(N_leaf,2) * 2^-256          = 2^-229.8302   (the memo's 2^-229.8)
  N_overlap  * 2^-256           = 2^-241.4153   (the 2^-241.42 row)
  N_node*N_leaf * 2^-512        = 2^-484.8307   (correction C-4)
  q * N_leaf * 2^-256           = q * 2^-242.4150
  [OK ] 2^-229.83 reproduces: got '-229.83'
  [OK ] 2^-241.42 reproduces: got '-241.42'
  [OK ] 2^-484.83 reproduces: got '-484.83'

  The q-term overtakes the collision term at q = 6,144 = 2^12.58.
  => pricing the flag at 2^-229.8 is right only for an adversary making
     fewer than 2^12.6 oracle queries.  [FINDING]
  The memo's stated MECHANISM for 2^-241.42 ('a digest must spell 24 fixed
  bytes') would give 2^-192 per pair, not 2^-241.42; the figure of record
  comes from the 32-byte SALT being uniform, counted over 24,571 objects:
     24 fixed bytes           -> 2^-192 per pair
     32 uniform salt bytes x 24571 objects -> 2^-241.4153
  [OK ] seam spec digest  = DOMAIN(28)+ctx(32)+8*u64+i32: got 128
  [OK ] general endpoint spec = DOMAIN(42)+ctx(32)+8*u64+i32: got 142
  [OK ] internal boundary spec = DOMAIN(43)+ctx(32)+9*u64+i32: got 151

